  "findings": [
    "Metacarpals 2 and 3 are about 2.4-2.5 SD shorter than the 1998 male radiographic means, and about 9-12 mm shorter than the independent 2025 CT means.",
    "Metacarpal 4 is also short (~1.6 SD; ~6.4 mm below both cited means).",
    "Metacarpals 1 and 5 are close to the 1998 male means; metacarpal 5 is also close to the 2025 CT mean.",
    "Most phalange spans are within 2 SD of the 1998 male sample; the hand-shortness signal is therefore concentrated much more strongly in metacarpals 2-4 than in the phalanges.",
    "The current M2/M3/M4 shortening is consistent with the independently measured short hand surface, so these bones should be reopened for the canonical skeleton rather than preserved merely to fit r95."
  ],
